    description: "OWNER DECISION: language=None stand-in fingerprints are emitted as bare 16-hex without a scheme label.\n\nSince PR 3 commit 497cbc3d5 (WI-tovog) they are minted by one factory, analyze/base.py mint_stand_in_fingerprint. They reach output: mitmproxy has 221 language=None nodes, all bare 16-hex (http 111, message_dispatch 47, js_module 29, subprocess_cli 23, message_queue 6, event_sourcing 5). ADR-0035 section 7 says every identity value carries a scheme-derived label but its table lists only hgfp2:; the spec's fingerprint bullet says this shape \"carries no hgfp2: prefix by design\"; SYMBOL_FINGERPRINT_SCHEME names a different algorithm. Options (/home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/pr3/agent5/RESULTS.md): (a) keep bare hex and write the exemption into ADR-0035 section 7; (b) a new scheme constant and label (e.g. hgstandinfp1:); (c) label as hgfp2: (wrong algorithm); (d) drop the values."  # b567
    fields: {}  # b567
